title: HitPilot
message: If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hentabli
    given-names: Hamza
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-24"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/hentablihamza/hitpilot"
url: "https://github.com/hentablihamza/hitpilot"
abstract: >-
  HitPilot is an open-source, auditable hit-triage and medicinal-chemistry
  copilot. It standardizes public screening libraries with RDKit, applies
  PAINS, Brenk, and NIH structural alerts, computes physicochemical properties
  and ChEMBL/PubChem novelty, selects diverse scaffolds, exposes a ChemMCP
  tool layer, joins an external docking or ML rescorer CSV, reports leak-checked
  virtual-screening enrichment, and writes a shareable med-chem dossier.
  All chemistry is computed on public LIT-PCBA, ChEMBL, and PubChem data.
keywords:
  - cheminformatics
  - drug-discovery
  - rdkit
  - virtual-screening
  - computational-chemistry
  - medicinal-chemistry
  - mcp
